updated_at":"2026-03-06T18:44:29Z","closed_at":"2026-03-06T18:44:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.stable.mono.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7800 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.12033.1030) - AMD Ryzen 5 7600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI made a simple subdivided cube with some shape keys as a test.\nWhen imported into Godot, the automatic LoDs change at much too close of a distance and trying to increase the LoD Bias seems to have absolutely no effect. The Model returns to normal when LoDs are disabled.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nimport a model\nobserve the distance that automatic LoDs change\nchange LoD bias\nno change in behaviour\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[lod-bug-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19566684/lod-bug-test.zip)\n\nin `cube_shapekey_test.tscn` you can zoom in and out to see the LoD change\nin `subdivided_cube.tscn` it seems just permanently stuck in a lower LoD. Reimporting without generating LoDs is the only way to return it to normal.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}